@startuml ZendaAuthFlow
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA

title Zenda -- Full Authentication Flow

actor Student
participant "Flutter App\n(AuthNotifier)" as App
participant "ApiClient\n(flutter_secure_storage)" as Client
participant "NestJS API\n/api/auth" as API
participant "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "SMTP / Email" as Mail

== Registration ==
Student -> App : fill name / email / password
App -> Client : POST /auth/register
Client -> API : { fullName, email, password }
API -> API : validate DTO (class-validator)
API -> API : bcrypt.hash(password, 10)
API -> DB : INSERT User (consentGiven=true)
API -> API : sign accessToken (15 min JWT)\nsign refreshToken (7 d JWT)
API -> DB : INSERT RefreshToken
API --> Client : { accessToken, refreshToken, user }
Client -> Client : secureStorage.write\n(access + refresh tokens)
Client --> App : AuthState.authenticated(user)
App --> Student : navigate to /dashboard

== Login (returning user) ==
Student -> App : email + password
App -> Client : POST /auth/login
Client -> API : { email, password }
API -> DB : SELECT User WHERE email
API -> API : bcrypt.compare(password, hash)
API -> API : sign new token pair
API -> DB : INSERT RefreshToken (revoke old ones)
API --> Client : { accessToken, refreshToken, user }
Client -> Client : persist tokens
Client --> App : AuthState.authenticated(user)

== Silent Token Refresh (on 401) ==
App -> Client : any authenticated request
Client -> API : Bearer [accessToken]
API --> Client : 401 Unauthorized (token expired)
Client -> API : POST /auth/refresh { refreshToken }
API -> DB : SELECT RefreshToken WHERE token
API -> API : validate not expired, sign new pair
API -> DB : DELETE old / INSERT new RefreshToken
API --> Client : { accessToken, refreshToken }
Client -> Client : overwrite stored tokens
Client -> API : retry original request
API --> Client : 200 OK

== Password Reset ==
Student -> App : Forgot password - enter email
App -> Client : POST /auth/forgot-password
Client -> API : { email }
API -> DB : INSERT PasswordResetToken (32-byte, 1h TTL)
API -> Mail : send reset link with token
Mail --> Student : email with reset link
Student -> App : click link - enter new password
App -> Client : POST /auth/reset-password { token, newPassword }
API -> DB : SELECT token, check not expired / not used
API -> API : bcrypt.hash(newPassword)
API -> DB : UPDATE User.passwordHash, mark token used
API --> Client : 204 No Content

== Logout ==
Student -> App : tap Logout
App -> Client : POST /auth/logout (Bearer)
Client -> API : revoke all refresh tokens for userId
API -> DB : DELETE RefreshTokens WHERE userId
API --> Client : 204 No Content
Client -> Client : secureStorage delete tokens
Client --> App : AuthState.unauthenticated()
App --> Student : navigate to /auth/login

@enduml
